            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="scale-notes">
            <div class="scale-note-col">
              <div class="gallery-label" style="margin-bottom:0.6rem">What each relationship says</div>
              <div class="sc-note-item"><div class="sc-dot" style="background:#7ec87e"></div><div class="sc-note-txt"><strong>Tree — 6 tiles.</strong> Larger than the player and the door. The player is inside an environment, not beside a prop.</div></div>
              <div class="sc-note-item"><div class="sc-dot" style="background:#c8a060"></div><div class="sc-note-txt"><strong>Door — 2 tiles tall.</strong> Taller than the player. It reads as a passage. Same height as the player reads as a wall mark.</div></div>
              <div class="sc-note-item"><div class="sc-dot" style="background:#6898c8"></div><div class="sc-note-txt"><strong>Window — 1 tile.</strong> Smaller than the door. The hierarchy signals building.</div></div>
              <div class="sc-note-item"><div class="sc-dot" style="background:#c8d8f0"></div><div class="sc-note-txt"><strong>Player — 1 tile, always.</strong> The fixed reference. Everything else is measured against this.</div></div>
